It is preferable if the following definitions are used to write theorems, corollaries, lemmas, etc.:
\begin{lemma}
A formulation of the lemma
\end{lemma}
Proof\\
\begin{theorem}
A formulation of the theorem
\end{theorem}
Proof\\

If you do not want to enumerate theorems, lemmas, propositions, etc. then the following definition would be used:
\begin{Lemma}
A formulation of the lemma
\end{Lemma}
Proof\\
\begin{Theorem}
A formulation of the theorem
\end{Theorem}
Proof\\

